There are only two guaranteed appearances of the Wizard in the dungeon;
originally in his tower, and on the Plane of Earth. New instances of
the Wizard (sometimes as double trouble) may appear from time to time.
There is no guarantee that the Wizard will appear at the Sanctum.
Besides the RNG whether or not you meet him depends on the time you
stay there; e.g. if you clear your way through the morgue by fighting
all monsters, then by fighting each of the monsters in the large area
around the temple, that will require a lot time (where the Wizard may
randomly can appear). If you level-teleport from the VS level down,
you may not need to pass the morgue, it may even happen that you land
inside the temple; in that case you save a lot of time and the Wizard
RND-trigger is less often checked for a new appearance.

Whenever the Wizard is arriving on a level where the Amulet is located
he teleports quite immediately close to the carrier. In the heat of
the fights in the Sanctum you may have missed that he had arrived and
immediately left you to get close to the High Priest in the Sanctum.
In that case I have also very often just missed his arrival since he
teleported away quickly; but you can hear that he's on the level by
the remote fighting noise of which you are informed by Nethack.

There are a couple of standard monsters in the Sanctum and a few in
the temple; 5 demons, 9 priests, 2 liches, and 3 vampires. As long as
you haven't genocided monsters or monster are not extinct you should
always find those in the Sanctum, besides the undead morgue residents
and some occasional random monsters.

The RNG is not nice to you, rather IME there are two possibilities for
what you call "unusual nice"; either (in case you have some weak point
in your set-up) he prepares you for some very frustrating death, or,
(in case that you are a comparably invincible[*] character), he grants
you a favour that you don't need anyway, to mentally prepare you for
his next chance to kill you (which might also be in a subsequent game
if it doesn't work out in the current one).

